  "hypothesis": "Map text is not truncated at embedded NUL in JS before dimensions/placement, unlike C dupstr-based parsing.",
  "expectedBehavior": "C writes6 floor cells with dimensions3x2; table frame10,6,3,2; centered frame39,11,3,2.",
  "observedBehavior": "JS writes8 floor cells with dimensions3x3; table frame10,6,3,3; centered frame39,9,3,3.",
  "witness": {
    "kind": "production_api",
    "scope": "Production special-level loader calls des.map table form at10,6, or its documented centered row-array counterpart to the C string form. Input bytes are ... newline ... newline NUL ... with two dots after NUL (hex2e2e2e0a2e2e2e0a002e2e). Both complete row array and C prefix are rectangular. Exact C lspo_map/mapfrag parser/dupstr execute with typed string/table readers and checked floor-terrain/selection adapters.",
    "limitations": [
      "API-scoped map construction only. Shipped levels containing embedded NUL are not attributed; no hidden-score or gameplay exposure claim. This is related to the accepted level-message/engraving C-string prefix cause, not a new independent repair identity.",
      "C executes exact lspo_map, mapfrag_fromstr/get/free, stripdigits, str_lines_maxlen and dupstr. Typed reader adapters supply exact string/table inputs; bytes are hex-decoded without truncation. The source dupstr/strlen execution, not a precomputed expected prefix, causes truncation. No full Lua interpreter is executed.",
      "Floor terrain conversion/writes and selection storage are checked adapters. They assert only dot terrain, lit0, in-bounds coordinates and selected cells; no metadata, lighting, arbitrary characters, room/themeroom placement, callback, finalization or RNG parity claim.",
      "JS des.map row-array form is the production documented counterpart of C string form. Plain JS scalar string is not its supported invocation. The final array has equal-width3 rows and the C prefix is a valid3x2 map; no invalid row-length setup supports the claim.",
      "Only mapfrag_fromstr:dupstr is scanner-bound. The C lspo_map scanner edge maps to a different exported JS helper, so it is left unreviewed; actual public wrapper source is cited separately."
    ]
  },
